Package: flickos-countme
Architecture: all
# flickos-branding: /usr/lib/flickos-release has the version that is sent.
# pkexec: enable/disable (countme-helper).
Depends: python3,
         flickos-branding,
         pkexec,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: anonymous weekly count of FlickOS installs
 Once a week a timer sends one request to the FlickOS counting server with
 only the FlickOS version and roughly how long ago it was installed (first
 week, first month, first half year, longer). No machine id, user or
 computer name, hardware or list of programs is sent, and the server keeps
 only the weekly counts. It tells the FlickOS developers how many computers
 run which version.
 .
 Nothing is sent in the live session. It is on by default (the installer
 says so), also on systems installed before it, until it is turned off.
 Settings -> Privacy or "flickos-countme disable" turns it off, and
 "flickos-countme show" prints exactly what is sent.
